    "setupNotes": [
      "Official 2.1.24 Space Age; 10 assembling machine 2 (6 copper cable, 4 electronic circuit), no modules, red belts, fast and bulk inserters, one substation. WEST: copper plates 540/min (upper entrance) and iron plates 360/min (lower entrance); both may arrive on both lanes, the blueprint side-loads each onto its own lane of the plate belt (row 4). EAST: one red belt exit on row 4, 360 electronic circuits/min, 180 per lane. Cable is handed machine to machine; keep the bulk arms (hand 2) at the outer cable machines and the fast arms at the middle one: the hand sizes fix the 2:1 cable split. Keep the plate filters on the input arms, the underground belt pairs and the dead-end curve at the east end of the plate belt. Supply electricity at the substation.",
      "Belt the exit east to the circuit entrances of the consumers; one red belt carries up to five copies (1,800/min). The exit holds 8 circuits when the consumer stops taking them, and every machine then stops.",
